  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015), CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast, Mon 10/26 09:00, St. Brigid. Steps done under RBC-RAD-07:\n- I placed the CT order (sr-t0001) and linked it to appointment appt-00001.\n- §1–2 (contrast allergy): His allergy list says \"anaphylaxis,\" but that was added in 2021 from his own account. The radiology report from the day of the reaction (2019-05-14) records hives and eyelid swelling with no airway or blood-pressure problems, and grades it moderate. So the policy calls for premedication, not \"no contrast.\" I ordered:\n  - prednisone 50 mg by mouth at 10/25 20:00, 10/26 02:00 and 10/26 08:00 (mr-t0002)\n  - diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth at 10/26 08:00 (mr-t0003)\n  He was told he needs a driver. Shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies aren't risk factors under the policy.\n- §4 (kidney check): He is 64 and has diabetes. His ED creatinines (1.94, then 1.46 on 10/16–17) were drawn during kidney injury and don't count. His 9/24 value is more than 30 days before the scan. I ordered a new creatinine to be drawn before the scan, by 10/26 08:30 (sr-t0005). The scan stays as booked; the radiologist reviews the result that day.\n- §6 (metformin): The ED summary shows kidney injury, so metformin 1000 mg twice daily (mr-00189) is on hold now, through at least 48 hours after the scan. I ordered a repeat creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006); this also covers the ED's request for repeat kidney tests. I gave you a task (task-t0007) to review that result and restart metformin only if it's normal.\n- I sent him portal instructions (comm-t0008): when to get the blood test, the medication timing, that he needs a driver, to stop metformin and not restart until told, to drink fluids, and when to seek urgent care. Arrival is 8:45.\n- A progress note citing RBC-RAD-07 is signed (doc-t0009).\n\nOpen item for you: I left the \"anaphylaxis\" allergy entry for iohexol (alg-00009) unchanged, though the 2019 report doesn't support it. Please review whether to correct it.",
